      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Buckets are not enough for NTM fluids. A §6Universal Fluid Tank§r holds 1,000 mB of any NTM fluid and is the standard way to move fluids by hand and to load them into machines. The §6Fluid Barrel§r holds 16,000 mB. §6Canisters§r are meant for liquid fuels.\n\nFor storage, place a §3Steel Barrel§r: it holds 16,000 mB, can be filled and emptied with containers or pipes, and accepts hot and corrosive fluids. Highly corrosive fluids eat through it, though, and turn it into a leaking §3Corroded Barrel§r.\n\nAll of them need aluminium plates, so you will want the combination oven running on cryolite first.",
